{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Wayfinding.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Wayfinding.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"wayfinding wayfinding","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Wayfinding.md","fileName":"Wayfinding.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Wayfinding","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Perception and Navigation]] [[Augmented Reality Navigation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Perception and Navigation","Augmented Reality Navigation","Navigation","Cognitive Map","Landmark","Virtual Environment","3D Travel","Cognitive Load","Spatial Knowledge","AR Route Visualization","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Wayfinding.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Wayfinding.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"wayfinding wayfinding","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Wayfinding.md","fileName":"Wayfinding.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Wayfinding","heading":"Wayfinding","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Wayfinding is the cognitive process of determining and following a route between an origin and a destination. It is the planning and decision-making component of [[Navigation]].\n\nThe user determines the current location, selects a path, maintains orientation, and builds or consults a [[Cognitive Map]]. Wayfinding aids support this mental work rather than moving the user directly. Examples include maps, signs, trails, compasses, reference objects, and [[Landmark]]s.\n\nIn a large or unfamiliar [[Virtual Environment]], wayfinding aids can be essential even when the [[3D Travel]] technique is efficient. Integrated aids can reduce [[Cognitive Load]] and strengthen [[Spatial Knowledge]].\n\nAn [[AR Route Visualization]] can place a path or decision cue directly onto the traveler's view of the physical environment. This reduces the transformation required from a separate map, but the route should still expose useful landmarks and orientation so the user does not become dependent on following an isolated arrow.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Perception and Navigation","Augmented Reality Navigation","Navigation","Cognitive Map","Landmark","Virtual Environment","3D Travel","Cognitive Load","Spatial Knowledge","AR Route Visualization","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Wayfinding.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Wayfinding.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"wayfinding wayfinding","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Wayfinding.md","fileName":"Wayfinding.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Wayfinding","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n[[augmentedreality_pearson.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Perception and Navigation","Augmented Reality Navigation","Navigation","Cognitive Map","Landmark","Virtual Environment","3D Travel","Cognitive Load","Spatial Knowledge","AR Route Visualization","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}